    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Driven by seasonal conditions enabling increased crossing attempts, frontline enforcers securing the border saw apprehensions surge from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March. This decisive action at the international boundary, a frontline where security is actively maintained, has been effective. Tough border policies have driven crossings to historic lows, demonstrating the strength of current enforcement measures despite the monthly spike.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Hero",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Even as enforcement action intercepted a surge in crossing attempts at the U.S. border, overall crossings remain suppressed by current enforcement measures, with apprehension authorities performing their duty. However, political inaction stalls critical support for those guarding the border, as elected officials yet to act decisively remain deadlocked in a legislative stalemate over funding. This impasse leaves the heroes on the front line without the resources they need.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Hero",
        "fragments": [
